stency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":0.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":0.3159041816043717,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.12935683923868457,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":89.7,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.04755977271611829,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":64.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.006499842102287601,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":58.1,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.010196768690534116,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":83.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.0034999999,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":2.3,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Invitation Homes Inc., is nation's premier single-family home leasing and management company, helping to expand housing through new development and strategic partnerships. Their purpose, Unlock the Power of Home, reflects their commitment to address America's housing needs by delivering high-quality living solutions and genuine care to those who choose the flexibility and value of leasing. Invitation Homes Inc. was incorporated in 6th June 2012 and is based in Dallas, United States.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Dallas B. Tanner | Co-Founder, CEO, President & Director | Age 44 | Compensation: $3.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $1.6M ranks in the below the sector median among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 13%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $559K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $16K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Invitation Homes Inc. is a large-cap real estate business with a $16.1B market cap on $2.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 1% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $963M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 35 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.05\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 11.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.1485740561755853},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Real Estate peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Real Estate sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 6% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Invitation Home (INVH) Up 4.4% Since Last Earnings Report: Can It Continue?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3036662/invitation-home-invh-up-4-4-since-last-earnings-report-can-it-continue?cid=CS-ZC-FT-realtime_blog-3036662","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795793427.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"How Invitation Homes Inc. (INVH) Affects Rotational Strategy Timing","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/24/How_Invitation_Homes_Inc._INVH_Affects_Rotational_Strategy_Timing_112626115202_1795711922.html","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795711922.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What Makes Invitation Homes (NYSE:INVH) A Notable Name Among Bluechip Stocks?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/bluechip/what-makes-invitation-homes-nyseinvh-a-notable-name-among-bluechip-stocks","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795196460.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Zacks Industry Outlook Highlights Invitation Homes, Essex Property and Equity LifeStyle","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.